   "text": {
    "L1": "A frog has a life story that begins in water.",
    "L2": "First come eggs, and then a baby frog called a tadpole hatches.",
    "L3": "A tadpole has a tail, but it is not a baby fish.",
    "L4": "Next, legs grow while the tail gets smaller.",
    "L5": "Finally, the tail goes and the tadpole becomes a frog.",
    "L6": "The frog hops on the wall, but the frogs hop together.",
    "L7": "The poem uses rhyming pairs such as wiggle and jiggle.",
    "L8": "Now put the frog's life stages in the order they happen."
   },
